# A hand-curated, property-diverse pool for decoy selection (offline).
#
# Why this file exists: an enrichment number is only as good as its decoys, and
# a decoy set that is not property-matched to the actives inflates every metric.
# Downloading DUD-E is not possible in this repository (no network in the test
# environment, and a vendor catalogue would not be redistributable), so the pool
# is written out by hand: common metabolites, drugs, fragments and amino acids
# chosen to span the property ranges of the demo library's actives (roughly
# 90-250 Da, LogP -3 to +3, 0-5 donors, 0-8 acceptors, 0-6 rotatable bonds).
#
# It is a *pool*, not a decoy set: `odock.decoys.match_decoys` picks the members
# that match each active on MW/LogP/HBD/HBA/RotB/charge within stated tolerances
# and rejects any that is topologically too similar to an active. Nothing here is
# claimed to be inactive against any target - see docs/LBVS.md.
#
